/**
 * @page topic_server_main Server Lifecycle
 * @ingroup module_server
 * @brief Server startup, listener ownership, connection callbacks, and shutdown.
 *
 * Server mode creates shared listeners and one `network_server_t`. TCP,
 * WebSocket, native QUIC, and WebTransport listeners feed the same connection
 * callback contract where enabled. The server application does not create a
 * separate receive/send thread pair for each protocol.
 *
 * @section server_main_start Startup
 *
 * Startup parses options, initializes crypto/media services, configures optional
 * QUIC/WebTransport endpoints, creates the network server, and starts listeners.
 * The server callback installs `client_info_t` state for each peer and begins
 * ACIP negotiation.
 *
 * @section server_main_run Run loop
 *
 * `network_server_run()` drives connection callbacks and backend I/O. Server
 * callbacks use `network_connection_transport()` and ACIP helpers; render and
 * audio workers publish outbound media without bypassing the transport layer.
 *
 * @section server_main_stop Shutdown
 *
 * Signal handlers only call `network_server_request_stop()`. After the run loop
 * returns, `network_server_stop()` drains connections and backend workers while
 * preserving dependencies if a join fails. The owner then destroys the server,
 * QUIC endpoints, media services, and UI in dependency order.
 *
 * @see topic_server_client
 * @see topic_network
 * @see topic_quic
 */
